---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Delete your data · b-mobile for Blipfoto · b-oss"
  description="How to delete the data b-mobile for Blipfoto handles, and where to delete a Blipfoto account."
  narrow
>
  <Hero label="Data deletion hero" title="Delete your data — b-mobile for Blipfoto">How to delete the data b-mobile for Blipfoto handles, and where to delete your Blipfoto
      account. b-mobile is an independent app built on Blipfoto's public API, and is not
      affiliated with or endorsed by Blipfoto.</Hero>

  <section
    class="block"
    style="border-top: none; padding-top: 0"
    data-screen-label="Data deletion body"
  >
    <h2>1. The notifications record</h2>
    <p>
      If you turned notifications on, b-push (the app's notification service) holds a record for
      each account: your Blipfoto user ID, an encrypted read-only access token, your device's
      push token, and your notification choices. To delete it, while your phone is online:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        In <strong>Settings</strong>, under <strong>b-mobile notifications</strong>, turn off
        both <strong>New comments</strong> and <strong>New notifications</strong> for the
        account; or
      </li>
      <li>
        In <strong>Accounts</strong>, open the account's options and choose
        <strong>Disconnect account</strong>.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Either deletes the record straight away. If you uninstall the app without doing this, the
      record is deleted automatically the next time b-push tries to reach your phone and Google
      reports the app gone.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Data kept only on your phone</h2>
    <p>
      Your access tokens (in Android's secure storage), settings, hidden members, drafts, photos
      waiting to upload and the picture cache are stored only on your phone and are not sent to
      the developer. Uninstalling the app removes them, as does
      <strong>Android Settings → Apps → b-mobile → Storage → Clear storage</strong>.
    </p>
    <p>
      On Android 10 and later, photos you download from your own entries are saved to
      <code>Pictures/b-mobile</code> and stay there after uninstalling. Delete them from your
      gallery or file manager like any other picture.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Your Blipfoto account and content</h2>
    <p>
      Your Blipfoto account, journal, entries, photos and comments are held by Blipfoto, not by
      b-mobile. Deleting a Blipfoto account is not available to apps like b-mobile; it is done
      on Blipfoto's website, in your
      <a href="https://www.blipfoto.com/settings/profile">Blipfoto account settings</a> (see
      also <a href="https://www.blipfoto.com/help">Blipfoto help</a>). In the app,
      <strong>Accounts</strong> → the account's options → <strong>Delete account</strong>
      opens that page.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you use b-mobile notifications, turn them off or disconnect the account in the app
      first (section 1), then delete your Blipfoto account.
    </p>

    <h2>More detail</h2>
    <p>
      The <a href="b-mobile-privacy.html">b-mobile privacy policy</a> describes everything the
      app handles. Questions can be sent to
      <a href="mailto:b-oss@salientpoint.co.uk">b-oss@salientpoint.co.uk</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
